                "senderName": "NWS Honolulu HI",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 7 at 11:11AM HST until September 7 at 2:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "FFWHFO\n\nThe National Weather Service in Honolulu has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nThe island of Kauai in Kauai County\n\n* Until 200 PM HST.\n\n* At 1111 AM HST, significant rises in water level have occurred\nalong the South Fork of the Wailua River over the past hour due to\nheavy rain upstream. While heavy rain is diminishing, additional\nrunoff is likely and could lead to flooding issues farther\ndownstream near the river mouth in Wailua. This warning replaces\nthe warning previously in effect for the north central portion of\nKauai including the Hanalei area.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Gauges reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nLihue, Kapaa, Princeville, Kilauea, North Fork Wailua Trails,\nWailua Homesteads, Hanalei, Wailua, Moloaa, Wainiha, Anahola and\nAlakai Swamp Trails.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
